# ============================================================================
# WHITELIST MODEL. Ignore everything; allow only what is deliberately public.
#
# Rationale: this repo is PUBLIC. A blacklist fails open — anything nobody
# thought to exclude gets published. A whitelist fails closed. Adding a file
# to the public surface must be a decision someone makes, not the default.
#
# Before adding an allow rule, ask: does this need to be public, or is it
# merely not embarrassing? Those are different tests.
# ============================================================================

# Ignore everything by default
*

# Directory traversal must stay open or nothing below matches
!*/

# --- The public surface ---------------------------------------------------

!.gitignore
!README.md
!LICENSE*

# The plugin itself — this is the artifact people install and read
!.claude-plugin/**
!agents/**
!commands/**
!skills/**
!playbooks/**
!templates/**

# Implementation and its tests
!scripts/**
!tests/**

# --- Never public, even if a rule above would otherwise match --------------

# Build noise
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Client and target data — hard rule 3. Engagements live in ~/engagements/.
*.secrets.env
.secrets.env
engagements/
evidence/
**/authorization/

# Root files that are deliberately curated, not merely tracked by habit.
!CLAUDE.md
!session.md

# status.md is withheld. Its "NOT enforced" list names exact, current,
# unfixed code-level gaps -- a usable map for anyone wanting to misuse the
# framework during a live engagement. It stays the authoritative internal
# record; it is not a public artifact.

# Documentation: allow the spec and the briefing, withhold the rest.
# NOTE: a parent-directory ignore cannot be selectively un-ignored, so these
# are targeted rules rather than `docs/` plus negations.
!docs/specs/**
!docs/REDGOLD-BRIEFING.md

# Findings about our own controls, a working harness hook-bypass technique,
# commercial analysis, legal exposure. None of it needs to be public.
docs/research/
docs/wiki/

# Superseded by status.md. A second stale copy of numbers that already went
# stale once is a liability, not signal.
docs/sessions/

# Client-facing demo material. Predates every disclaimer added since; its
# enforcement claims were never re-checked against the nine controls moved to
# NOT enforced. Withheld pending review, not because it is unflattering.
docs/demo/
